From bd9b5397f5d8ea494b4f2f66278a65033c9af594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: u1131128 <hipac1@lsalab.cs.nthu.edu.tw>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:06:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Collapse only the spatial loops of the per-variable copy
 and difference kernels

Every hot copy/difference kernel collapsed (variable, z, y, x) into one index space, so each element paid
for a 64-bit div/mod index recovery and a derived-type descriptor walk. Collapse the three spatial loops and
run the variable loop sequentially inside the thread; per-element arithmetic is unchanged (bit-identical).

Backport of upstream #2087 (AppleChen17, merged 2026-10-24): the q_cons copy, the x/y/z flux differences,
the finalize copies and the WENO input pack. Same pattern extended here to the dual-pass and cylindrical
flux differences, the cylindrical finalize copies, the WENO1 copies, the RK update and the u-interface
alpha*div(u) source term (its face velocities are loaded once per cell).
